<p>The United States, Iran and regional mediators are discussing a possible two-phase arrangement that would begin with a 45-day ceasefire in the Iran war, according to Axios as cited across the provided reports. The idea is to create breathing room for talks on a permanent end to the fighting, with negotiators focusing on reopening the Strait of Hormuz and addressing Iran’s enriched uranium stockpile. The diplomatic push comes as President Trump moved his deadline on reopening the Strait of Hormuz from Monday to Tuesday, while warning of strikes on Iranian civilian infrastructure if shipping is not restored. The reports say mediators from Pakistan, Egypt and Turkey have carried several proposals, alongside messages between US envoy Steve Witkoff and Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi. So far, Tehran has not accepted any proposal and has publicly denied seeking a ceasefire.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/93BxrS8NBnfghcvrMOJXoUb8tiyO6oiKR1J39X_c1RescmE5zDV4jqzdrYZ_4Q0YqaiFxPLwUT_caEkpc6rZ5lW4ddpyBLyJ-hsvcDVIUMf6tUX-kq2-bwxNmDEVw36K7_pvhTxynXzoBLV85bGWrhB1E2ogJUhQqMhoQLD7mmmJ5dLsJvxmiJbTTIkyMScO' alt='Image published with coverage of reported US-Iran ceasefire talks.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Mediator channels: The reported contacts are moving through Pakistani, Egyptian and Turkish intermediaries instead of direct public talks, a sign that diplomacy is still active even as the military deadline nears.</li><li>Two-phase plan: Under the reported framework, the initial 45-day pause could be extended if needed while negotiators work toward a permanent settlement.</li><li>Short odds: Reports described the chances of securing a deal before the latest deadline as slim, underscoring how little time remains for a breakthrough.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States: President Trump said Washington was negotiating with Tehran while tying diplomacy to a deadline for restoring shipping through the Strait of Hormuz. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637410-us-seeks-ceasefire-with-iran/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Iran: Tehran has denied seeking a ceasefire and rejected President Trump’s claim that it was asking for one. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/middle-east-conflict-end-to-iran-war-in-sight-45-day-ceasefire-being-discussed-says-report-11316235#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Regional mediators: Pakistani, Egyptian and Turkish intermediaries are reportedly trying to shape a phased arrangement that starts with a temporary halt and could open space for a permanent deal. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-iran-and-mediators-make-push-for-45-day-ceasefire-axios-reports/article70828810.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637410-us-seeks-ceasefire-with-iran/'>Mediators pushing for 45-day truce in Iran war – Axios</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/middle-east-conflict-end-to-iran-war-in-sight-45-day-ceasefire-being-discussed-says-report-11316235#publisher=newsstand'>End To Iran War In Sight? 45-Day Ceasefire Being Discussed, Says Report</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-iran-and-mediators-make-push-for-45-day-ceasefire-axios-reports/article70828810.ece'>U.S., Iran and mediators make push for 45-day ceasefire, Axios reports</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-iran-and-mediators-make-push-for-45-day-ceasefire-axios-reports'>US, Iran and mediators make push for 45-day ceasefire, Axios reports</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>